  "name": "Interior-quadratic glob: '*' + long-run + '*' deny Resource vs cap-length allow Resource",
  "note": "Every Action/Resource string is <= LIMITS.MAX_STRING_LENGTH (2048) and the whole document is far under MAX_BYTES, so validate() ACCEPTS it (validate.ok=true) - a per-string cap is no defense. The Deny Resource is the INTERIOR two-star form '*'+'a'*1023+'b'+'*': a long literal run placed BETWEEN two stars. Iteration-1's matcher only anchored the FIRST and LAST '*'-delimited segments, so this interior run was re-scanned by findSegFrom() from EVERY text offset against the 2048-char Allow Resource -> the exact O(n*m) quadratic the story claimed to remove (the story's tests only ever exercised the single-star SUFFIX form, which was anchored, so the interior case sailed through untested). The deny-coverage nested loops (applyDenyToActions -> denyResourceCoverage -> allowRes.every x denyStmt.resources.some) multiply the per-call cost. With the linear (Shift-And) interior matcher this analyzes in tens of ms; under the old quadratic it took seconds and grew ~4x per 2x size. It must NEVER hang and NEVER return a COMPLETE (ok:true, incomplete:false) clean-looking verdict after a long run.",
